# Packaging is controlled entirely by the "files" allowlist in package.json.
#
# This file is intentionally rules-only-comments. It exists so that npm does
# not fall back to .gitignore as the ignore source, because .gitignore excludes
# dist/ and build/ - artifacts the published package depends on.
#
# Do not add exclude rules here. The failure mode is documented in
# @digitaldefiance/node-rs-accelerate: version 0.1.2 published a package that
# could not be loaded at all, because its .npmignore excluded src/ and build/
# while dist/ required a native addon from build/ that could not be rebuilt
# from the tarball either. Express what ships as an allowlist in package.json
# instead, where omissions are visible in a diff.
#
# scripts/verify-pack.sh exists to prove the allowlist is sufficient. Run it
# before every publish.
